# RUN: llc -mtriple=mncore2 %s -o - | FileCheck %s
#
# G1: fbfn (single-precision block-float conversion) numeric golden.
#
# `fbfn` is a 4-cycle ALU expression at LONGWORD access width (SDM 3.6.12.12:
# one longword per PE per cycle for d/f/g). One instruction therefore
# converts four per-PE longwords; each longword holds two independent
# 32-bit words, and each word joins the four PEs of its MAB into one
# 4-word block that shares a common exponent.
#
#   cycle c reads longword (src_addr/2 + c), writes longword (dst_addr/2 + c)
#
# The conversions follow SDM 4.4, block size 4, mantissa field 23 bits with
# an EXPLICIT leading one: the bit pattern is decoded as
#     (-1)^s * 2^(e-127) * sum_{j=1..23} 2^(1-j) M_j,
# so the BF pattern of 1.0 (common exponent 0) is 0x3FC00000, which IEEE
# would read as 1.5. The raw bit patterns below are never IEEE values.
#
# Input pattern (per plane k, MAB m, local PE q; written as one longword
# per PE into L1B plane k and distributed by l1bmd):
#   m=0  hi = {1,2,3,4},              lo = {8,0.5,0,1+2^-23}
#   m=1  hi = 1.0,                    lo = {1.999...,1,1,1}   (carry bump)
#   m=2  hi = 0,                      lo = {inf,-2,1.5,subnormal}
#   m=3  hi = lo = {1+2^-23,1+2^-22,1+3*2^-23,1}   (round-half-even ties)
#   m>3  plain normal patterns derived from (k,m,q)
# Every exponent field except zero/subnormal and infinity is shifted by k, so
# the four cycles also differ in the data (not just the address).
#
# Measured map (gpfn3, 2026-11-04; scripts/check_mau_bfn.py models SDM 4.4
# and matches every cell): the block is per MAB, the two words of one
# longword are two independent blocks, and the cycle progression above holds.
# Width 2 also works (only the MSB longword of each 2-longword access is
# used), but width 1 is the SDM-native throughput form.
#
# d set/get spec: [3:0]mem (1=GRF0 6=L1B), [20:4]addr(word), [28:21]nwords
#   L1B@<a> n1 = 6 | (a << 4) | (1 << 21)
#   GRF0@0 n32 = 1 | (32 << 21) = 67108865

--- |
  target triple = "mncore2"
  define void @mau_bfn() { ret void }
...
---
